{
  "notes": "IBPS Clerk cutoffs are **state-wise and category-wise** — there is no all-India cutoff — and are reproduced here from IBPS result notices via the sources listed on each entry; decimals may differ slightly between reproductions, and the IBPS PDF on ibps.in is always canonical. Two scales matter: **Prelims out of 100** (qualifying — sectional minimums plus a state-wise shortlist; score discarded afterwards) and **Mains out of 200, reported on a normalised scale out of 100** — and since there is **no interview**, the mains cutoff **is** the final selection cutoff for the merit list. Do not be surprised when a reserved-category cutoff sits **above** the general one (for example Madhya Pradesh prelims 2024: SC 74.5 against UR 73) — category-wise vacancy counts differ hugely by state and some categories shortlist against very few seats. Cut-offs swing between states (recent prelims: mid-40s in Gujarat and Maharashtra, mid-80s in Chandigarh and Uttarakhand), so always benchmark against **your state's** last two cycles, not the national range. The mains pattern changed recently, so mains cutoffs before and after the change are only loosely comparable.",
